PROPOSED — NOT APPLIED. Lane TO, #276, P-274-3 + s275-D5.
Target: knowledge/components/meta.schema.json
Decision: D-3 on REVIEW-tie-off-2026-09-15-v1.html.

ONE new field: `edges.obeys`. It is a new EDGE TYPE inside the existing KG parse
layer, not a new top-level property — `edges` is the layer that exists for exactly
this (typed, resolvable node references), the explorer and gen_kg_edges.py already
read it, and adding a top-level `obeys` would create a second home for a fact the
graph already knows how to hold.

Two enabling clauses come with it, both SCOPED so nothing else widens:

  1. a new `definitions.obeysEdge` — same {ref, $note} shape as `definitions.edge`
     but with a ref pattern that admits `rule:` and `ux:` (both LIVE node kinds:
     `rule:` landed at #274 under s274-D8, `ux:` at #275 under s275-D4), plus a
     `$why` string. The shared `definitions.edge` is NOT touched, so `containedBy`
     still cannot point at a rule.
  2. `edges.$obeys-contract` — one string, the provenance sentence, so a reader of
     the meta alone can tell an AUTHORED edge from a generated one.

`$why` is REQUIRED on obeysEdge. That is the whole point of s274-D12 and s269-D5:
the durable route is authored, and an edge with no sentence attached is inference
wearing a ref.

